#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# implicit_region

#% text
# `implicit_region(cond, [x, y, ...])` is the region of the points whose coordinates satisfy the condition `cond`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Conditions are inequalities, equations and their combinations with `and`, `or` and `not`.

#% item
# Membership substitutes the point into the condition; bounds and measures of implicit regions are computed numerically.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The unit disk as a condition:

#% cell
r = implicit_region(x^2 + y^2 <= 1, [x, y])

#% text
# Membership:

#% cell
region_member(r, [1/2, 1/2])
#% output
#= true

#% text
# Its area, numerically:

#% cell
region_measure(r)
#% output
#= 3.1415939138804427

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Bounds of a rotated quartic region:

#% cell
region_bounds(implicit_region(x^4 - x*y + y^4 <= 1, [x, y]))
#% output
#= [[-1.1150447368259129, 1.1150447368259129], [-1.1150447368259129, 1.1150447368259129]]

#% text
# Drawn over its bounds:

#% cell
region_plot(implicit_region(x^2 + y^2 <= 1 and x > 0, [x, y]))
#% output
#= image("implicit_region.files/implicit_region-5.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `region_member`, `region_plot`, `parametric_region`
